## Rules
- Unless the inputs say otherwise: storey height 3.0 m, exterior walls 300 mm, interior walls 120 mm, slabs 200 mm.
- One level per storey, named "Ground Floor", "First Floor", …
- Doors 900×2100, windows 1200×1200 with 900 sill, unless shown otherwise.
- Create spaces/rooms named from drawing text where available.
- Do not invent elements the inputs don't support.
- Metres, IFC4. Every element must be contained in a storey.
- List every assumption in `output/assumptions.md` (it is shown publicly next to the model).

## Deliver — the operator tells you which route

### Route A — Revit (via the Revit MCP)
1. The operator has opened the IFCWise template and linked the inputs as underlays.
2. Create levels, then walls, floors, roof, doors, windows and rooms with the Revit MCP, using the
   coordinates in `prepared/*.geometry.json` where available (convert drawing units to metres).
3. Stop and report; the operator checks the model and exports IFC4 Reference View to `output/model.ifc`.

### Route B — model spec (no Revit)
Write `output/model-spec.json`, then run `npm run tools -- build {{ job.id }}` (it builds `output/model.ifc`
and validates it). Format, all lengths in metres; wall `start`/`end` are the wall centre line, opening
`offset` is measured along the wall from `start`:
```json
{
  "project": "{{ job.title }}",
  "defaults": {"wallThickness": 0.3, "storeyHeight": 3.0, "slabThickness": 0.2},
  "storeys": [
    {"name": "Ground Floor", "elevation": 0.0, "height": 3.0,
     "slab": {"outline": [[0, 0], [10, 0], [10, 12], [0, 12]]},
     "walls": [
       {"start": [0, 0], "end": [10, 0], "thickness": 0.3,
        "openings": [{"type": "door", "offset": 2.0, "width": 0.9, "height": 2.1},
                     {"type": "window", "offset": 5.0, "width": 1.2, "height": 1.2, "sill": 0.9}]}
     ],
     "spaces": [{"name": "Living", "outline": [[0.15, 0.15], [5, 0.15], [5, 11.85], [0.15, 11.85]]}]}
  ],
  "roof": {"outline": [[0, 0], [10, 0], [10, 12], [0, 12]], "thickness": 0.2}
}
```
Only flat roofs are supported by `build`; describe pitched roofs in `assumptions.md` (or use Route A).

### Both routes
- Write `output/assumptions.md`.
- `npm run tools -- validate {{ job.id }}` must pass (warnings are OK if explained in the assumptions).
